s/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1461:survives unchanged — anything the program did not observe is not the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1579:facts are ordinary datoms — using `dao.lease.md`'s vocabulary unchanged,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1595:or `:dao.lease/event`, each with `dao.lease.md`'s required keys, unchanged.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1806:Recovery also retains a complete codec snapshot when legacy fork bytes\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1807:omit transitive dependencies; the published version-0 bytes stay unchanged.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2103:  program wrote, unchanged and uninterpreted. A program value that\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2187:- The lease fact is unchanged. The binding is a separate fact, so a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2242:  bound it is still written, carrying the unchanged epoch.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2273:  the tenure, leaves the epoch unchanged, and permanently exhausts\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2341:target's DaoStream outcome map, unchanged. A terminal refusal is a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2342:result, recorded and replayed unchanged, but only when the atomic\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2392:predecessor's, unchanged. Only that accepted completion is an edge:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2515:`closed`, `invalid-descriptor`, …) are surfaced unchanged inside the UCF\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2586:  canonical-byte equality; the conflict decision is unchanged.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2621:  A front reply's `:yin.k/answer` is the landed answer unchanged\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2782:lane; due renewals and pending requests still send or retry unchanged. Inbound\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2787:durable release intent before sending and unchanged cleanup retries until\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3072:   unchanged on `:put`, `:ffi-request`, and `:link-request`, and the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3129:   `:suspended` with tenure, quarantine, and dedup state unchanged,\n   487\t\n   488\t**Lift, `act`.** From the kernel's wait entry with `:resume-mode\n   489\t:write-result` (payload `:image :site-pc :pc :frames :regs :live\n   490\t:continuation :dest :store-of`, v2 amendment §5.3):\n   491\t\n   492\t1. `A` = the A the image row of the entry's `:image` was derived from\n   493\t   (the kernel's code space is keyed by A after phase 5; R is its\n   494\t   checksum).\n   495\t2. relative `pc` = the entry's `pc` minus the image row's offset\n   496\t   (`image-row`/`absolute-pc`, `debruijn/register.cljc:326-337`); R's pcs\n   497\t   are A's, so this is the canonical pc.\n   621\t`(mapv Wᵢ (stack-layout_{Aᵢ} (dec pcᵢ)))`, then `slice(current) =\n   622\t(mapv W (stack-layout (dec pc)))`; `:continuation` = for each `fᵢ`\n   623\t`{:return-pc (+ offᵢ (a->h_{Aᵢ} (dec pcᵢ)) 1) :frames (§4.4 from Eᵢ)\n   624\t:stack-base (running length of the slices before slice(fᵢ))\n   625\t:store-of …}`; `:format stack/format-tag`; `:segment`/`:hash` the\n   626\treceiver's. `stack-restore` then conjes the delivered value onto\n   627\t`:stack` at `:pc`, which is the `:push`-free position after the parking\n   628\tinstruction, exactly where H expects the result.\n   629\t\n   630\t**Lower, `tail`, and the tail-completion seam.** Today the stack kernel\n   631\tresumes a parked host effect at the entry's `pc` by pushing the value\n   632\t(`stack-restore`, `:566`); for a **tail** call that resumes the body at\n   633\t`a->h(site)+1`, which then runs the layout syntax after the tail call\n   634\t(for a tail call in operand position: the remaining pushes and the\n   635\tenclosing call) **before** reaching `:return`. That is not the canonical\n   636\tthrough-return delivery (frozen §2.4, §4.1 \"effectful call, tail\":\n   637\tdelivery **through return** against `K`). The layout therefore cannot\n   638\tlower a canonical `tail` into today's stack kernel. **PROPOSED, gated\n   639\t(§8.3 slice 6c-pre):** the stack kernel gains a tail-completion seam:\n   640\tits park-entry builders mark an entry whose parking instruction is a\n   641\ttail `:call` with `:resume-mode :return-result` (the register kernel's\n   642\texisting vocabulary, `register.cljc:458-468`), and `stack-restore`\n   643\tdelivers such an entry by the **return transition** (pop the top frame,\n   644\ttruncate `:stack` to its base, push the value, restore its `frames`,\n   645\t`store-of` and `return-pc`; halt with the value when `K` is empty) instead\n   646\tof resuming at `pc`. Lowering a canonical `tail` then produces\n   647\t`{:image row-of-A :pc (+ off (a->h site) 1) :resume-mode :return-result\n   648\t:stack (concat of K slices) :frames [] :store-of nil :continuation …}`;\n   649\tthe `:frames`/`:store-of` values are unobservable (the return transition\n   650\treplaces them) and the harness checks that (§5.6 item 8). File:\n   651\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (not a 4b or phase-5 file); the\n   785\t`:591-603`); `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (a register kernel stepped one\n   786\tinstruction past a `:const`, asked to lift); `:yin.k/non-portable\n   787\t:reason-mismatch` (the `:observe` hold, `:675-692`); and the validator's\n   788\t**membership tampers**, each a row-set edit of a valid body before\n   789\tlower: a window with an extra live key → `:window-extra`; a live key\n   790\tremoved → `:window-missing`; `rd` added → `:window-self`; `rd` replaced\n   791\tby another register → `:destination`; a return frame's `pc` moved after\n   792\ta tail call → `:return-site`; a reason the site does not admit →\n   793\t`:reason-mismatch`; a `:tail` row given a fourth slot → `:frame-shape`;\n   794\tthe `[:lit nil]` of row 22 dropped → `:window-missing`; a `:reified`\n   795\tact whose `pc−1` is not a capture → `:captured-site`; a parked act whose\n   796\t`pc−1` is not `:park` → `:parked-site`; a binding of `x` in row 21's `E`\n   797\tchanged to `98` → `:free-env-mismatch`. **A changed live value**\n   798\t(e.g. `\"A\"` → `\"Z\"` in row 1's window) is not a membership defect and is\n   799\tnot expected to be refused: it is tested by **execution parity** (the\n   800\tlowered run's result differs from the reference), as the review ruled.\n   801\t\n   802\t### 5.3 Lanes\n   803\t\n   804\tThe `:semantic-register` lane's wait entries are canonical frames plus\n   805\tengine fields. The de Bruijn lanes load `(:image (derive/stack-image v))`\n   806\tand `(:image (derive/register-image v))` of `v = (:vector (project P))`\n   807\tthrough `dvm/create-vm`/`rvm/create-vm`, run to the safepoint and lift\n   808\tthrough `layout/lift-act`/`lift-tail`; the stack lane's tail rows (6,\n   809\t9, 12, 20) require the seam of §4.3 and are gated on 6c-pre.\n   810\t\n   811\t### 5.4 Laws\n   812\t\n   813\t1. **Reference parity**: result and effect trace of the lowered,\n   814\t   satisfied machine equal the reference run (`reference`/`handed-off`,\n   815\t   `:368-401`).\n   987\t   (twenty-four rows, named by kind); plus `first-defect-is-structural`:\n   988\t   a frame with a malformed `K` **and** a bad window reports `:k-shape`.\n   989\t4. `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member`: row 22's frame\n   990\t   validates with the nil key present; the same frame with the key\n   991\t   removed is `:window-missing`.\n   992\t5. `frame-test/worked-example-saved`: on `:worked-example`, a frame at pc\n   993\t   4 with window `{1 <f>}` and `rd 2` validates; `{1 <f> 2 x}` is\n   994\t   `:window-self`; `{}` is `:window-missing`; `{1 <f> 3 x}` is\n   995\t   `:window-extra` (`saved(4, 2) = {1}`, `analysis_test.cljc:131-139`).\n   996\t6. `frame-test/free-env-mismatch`: row 21's frame with `task :free-env\n   997\t   {x 99}` validates; with `{x 98}` or `{}` it is `:free-env-mismatch`;\n   998\t   a binding `y` present in `E` but absent from `free-env` and not\n   999\t   lexically bound is `:free-env-mismatch`.\n  1000\t7. `rows-test/bijection`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` and the converse\n  1001\t   are identities on every frame of item 2, nil-valued keys included.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'version.?0|version.?1|version.?2|legacy|two paths|vector.to.datoms|normaliz' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -35; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md | sed -n '704,750p;780,790p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md | sed -n '355,421p;500,512p;842,868p;752,782p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc | sed -n '310,345p'; rg -n ':prim/conj|conj|:=' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'version.?0|version.?1|version.?2|legacy|two paths|vector.to.datoms|normaliz' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -35; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md | sed -n '704,750p;780,790p'; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md | sed -n '355,421p;500,512p;842,868p;752,782p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc | sed -n '310,345p'; rg -n ':prim/conj|conj|:=' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"39:`:yin.k/version 1` adds the custody header, the operation-sequence state,\n42:no version-1 code is landed and it closes no blocker.\n121: :yin.k/contract    {:yin.code/contract \"v3\" :yin.k/version 0}   ; S7.3.3\n183: :yin.k/contract      {:yin.code/contract \"v3\" :yin.k/version 0}\n227:`:address-mismatch`, and, under version 1, `:unprotected-pending` and\n234::yin.k/version 0}`: the amendment changes handoff data and composition\n253:that speaks only version 0 refuses a version-1 body by this gate and\n258:writer. A version-0 body stays valid under this contract and is never\n259:upgraded to fenced custody, by a resumer or by a carrier. A version-0\n261:version-0 body establishes nothing. A reader that speaks version 1\n262:keeps these fork semantics for a version-0 body exactly, and refuses\n263:a version-0 body as `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` when exclusive custody\n264:is required. Version 0 is fork only and version 1 is exclusive only.\n266:**Version 1** is the fenced-custody grammar. A version-1 root body of\n289:  are required. The policy is exactly `:yin.k/exclusive`: version 1\n290:  has no fork form, and fork uses version 0.\n384:- **Normalization gate.** The falsy `:gensym` prefix is not yet normalized\n387:  address is accepted, both paths must use one normalization rule, or\n503:§7.3.2 normalizes away.\n513:Loading a fetched vector has two paths, and both are specified. The\n521:datoms, as a foreign engine would. The two paths are a conformance\n876:hold for both body versions of 7.2.1; operation ids are version 1.)\n941:  normalization invariant is specified and proved; M-next D tests\n966:- `:yin.k/phase` and `:yin.k/parent` are required under version 1.\n967:  A version-0 entry without a phase reads as `:running`.\n969:  for version 0 as well. The landed version-0 reader breaches both;\n972:*Operation ids ride on retained writes (version 1).* Three variants\n1781:A `nil` header lifts today's version-0 fork; a header lifts version 1,\n1790:`:yin.k/export-recovery` with format version 1, using the handoff value/cell\n1806:Recovery also retains a complete codec snapshot when legacy fork bytes\n1807:omit transitive dependencies; the published version-0 bytes stay unchanged.\n1808:For version 1, the module-store fixed point is a correctness repair:\n1844:origin at all is a version-0 result under a `nil` header); install\n1845:children carry no header. Before answering `:ok`, a version-1 root\n2037:### 7.7.8 Fenced custody, version 1: sequence, envelope, epoch binding\n   704\t\n   705\t**Lift** (reference machine): refuse unless quiescent; number cells (§6);\n   706\twalk waits, parked records, the slice, module stores, the result and\n   707\teach install child, emitting rows and the census; refuse by path as UCF\n   708\t§7.5.4 and §7.2.1 specify. The nested carrier's value table\n   709\t(`:yin.k/values`) has no counterpart, sharing being Merkle; its cell\n   710\ttable becomes the census.\n   711\t\n   712\t**Lower**: §8 in order, then restore.\n   713\t\n   714\tThe laws, with the domains the Architect's finding 12 requires:\n   715\t\n   716\t- **Canonical round trip.** For every valid, canonical (§6-numbered)\n   717\t  version-3 state `S` in the semantic profile **for which `lower(S)`\n   718\t  succeeds** (adequate composition, resource and admission inputs; a\n   719\t  refusal is not a counterexample), and with no execution between lower\n   720\t  and lift, `lift(lower(S)) = S` by root id under the **fresh-receiver\n   721\t  reconstruction context**: the receiver's id counter is 0 so\n   722\t  `max(local, carried)` is the carried value; occurrence, origin and the\n   723\t  custody arm are supplied to the lift from the restored task's own\n   724\t  record, not minted; cell bodies and op-ids are carried verbatim; the\n   725\t  lift's §6 numbering undoes resource remapping. Outside that context\n   726\t  (a receiver with a larger counter, or any step taken) the law does not\n   727\t  apply and native equivalence is the claim.\n   728\t- **Native observational equivalence.** `lower(lift(m))` need not equal\n   729\t  `m` as native state (fresh ids, seals, private keys); under equivalent\n   730\t  external inputs it must preserve the next observable step, the wait\n   731\t  set and its order, the result, and the effect trace.\n   732\t- **Cross-engine.** Running the corpus to each safepoint on an engine\n   733\t  that implements canonical semantic-VM execution yields, under\n   734\t  controlled composition identities (occurrence, origin, resource\n   735\t  descriptors fixed by the harness), the same version-3 row set the\n   736\t  reference machine yields.\n   737\t- **Legacy correspondence.** Versions 0, 1 and 2 are lowered directly by\n   738\t  their own version-aware readers, keeping their addresses and custody\n   739\t  bindings (§10.8). Normalization into version 3 is a separate tool and\n   740\t  is **partial**: a legacy body normalizes with semantic preservation\n   741\t  (same lowered machine under native equivalence) or refuses with one\n   742\t  of this carrier's named refusals (`:byte-string`, `:metadata`, a\n   743\t  profile version 3 does not yet support); it never substitutes a\n   744\t  version-3 address for an admitted legacy checkpoint. Exact mutual\n   745\t  inversion is required only between version 3 and its one canonical\n   746\t  nested projection (§10.3).\n   747\t\n   748\tThe UCF §7.11 harness gains one assertion per law. During transition the\n   749\tStage D/E corpus, re-encoded through the canonical projection, is the\n   750\toracle for the first law.\n   780\t   reified capture has no pending; a parked reference resolves in task\n   781\t   context.\n   782\t6. **Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before any implementation\n   783\t   brief claims heterogeneous execution conformance, and not drafted\n   784\t   here: admitted values, numeric behaviour, key equality, metadata,\n   785\t   resource and profile requirements, refusal sets, and safepoint\n   786\t   reconstruction obligations. Slot losslessness alone does not\n   787\t   establish execution parity, and version 3, like version 2, does not\n   788\t   translate between kernels.\n   789\t\n   790\tAnswers 7–9 are the Architect's (round 2) and are adopted:\n   355\t\n   356\t| # | Rule | Kind |\n   357\t|---|---|---|\n   358\t| S1 | `frame` is a map; `:yin.k/state` is `:act` or `:tail`; an `act` has exactly the keys `:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/pc :yin.k/env :yin.k/window :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k` plus optionally `:yin.k/pending`; a `tail` exactly `:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/site :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k` plus optionally `:yin.k/pending` | `:frame-shape` |\n   359\t| S2 | `:yin.k/k` is a vector; every element is a map with exactly `:yin.k/frame-type :yin.k/segment :yin.k/pc :yin.k/env :yin.k/window :yin.k/rd`, `:yin.k/frame-type` is `:return` | `:k-shape` (path `[:yin.k/k i]`) |\n   360\t| S3 | every `:yin.k/window` present (the act's, each return frame's) is a map whose keys are exact non-negative integers (on the wire: sorted ascending, unique) and whose values are `V` | `:window-representation` |\n   361\t| S4 | every `:yin.k/env` present is `{:yin.k/bindings {S V …}}` optionally with `:yin.k/store-of M`; `:yin.k/deliver` is a map | `:env-shape` / `:deliver-shape` |\n   362\t\n   363\t**Code (every frame).**\n   364\t\n   365\t| # | Rule | Kind |\n   366\t|---|---|---|\n   367\t| C1 | `:yin.k/segment` of the frame and of every return frame names a key of `code` | `:segment` |\n   368\t| C2 | an `act`'s `pc` and every return frame's `pc` satisfy `0 < pc < (count v)`; a `tail`'s `site` satisfies `0 ≤ site < (count v)` | `:pc-bounds` |\n   369\t| C3 | `body(pc−1) = body(pc)` for the act and every return frame (no body ends in a parking instruction, frozen §3.4 rule 6) | `:pc-body` |\n   370\t\n   371\t**The current activation (`act` only; a `tail` skips A1-A6).**\n   372\t\n   373\t| # | Rule | Kind |\n   374\t|---|---|---|\n   375\t| A1 | `inst(pc−1)` is one of `:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation`, or a `:call` with `tail?` false | `:site` |\n   376\t| A2 | `(:yin.k/rd deliver) = (code/rd inst(pc−1))` and `deliver = {:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd r}` exactly | `:destination` / `:deliver` |\n   377\t| A3 | every window key `< k(body(pc))` | `:window-scope` |\n   378\t| A4 | `rd ∉ (keys window)` | `:window-self` |\n   379\t| A5 | `(set (keys window)) ⊆ (analysis/saved a pc rd)` | `:window-extra` |\n   380\t| A6 | `(analysis/saved a pc rd) ⊆ (set (keys window))` | `:window-missing` |\n   381\t\n   382\t**The tail site (`tail` only).**\n   383\t\n   384\t| # | Rule | Kind |\n   385\t|---|---|---|\n   386\t| T1 | `inst(site)` is a `:call` with `tail?` true; `deliver = {:yin.k/deliver :return}` exactly | `:site` / `:deliver` |\n   387\t\n   388\t**Return frames (every frame, each `K[i]`).**\n   389\t\n   390\t| # | Rule | Kind |\n   391\t|---|---|---|\n   392\t| K1 | `inst(frame.pc−1)` in `frame.segment` is a `:call` with `tail?` false | `:return-site` |\n   393\t| K2 | `frame.rd = (code/rd inst(frame.pc−1))` | `:return-destination` |\n   394\t| K3 | every key of `frame.window` `< k(body(frame.pc))`; `frame.rd ∉ keys`; `(set (keys frame.window)) = (analysis/saved aₛ frame.pc frame.rd)` in that segment's analysis, reported as `:return-window-scope` / `:return-window-self` / `:return-window-extra` / `:return-window-missing` | as named |\n   395\t\n   396\t**Environments (every `E`: the act's and each return frame's).**\n   397\t\n   398\t| # | Rule | Kind |\n   399\t|---|---|---|\n   400\t| E1 | no binding key is reserved (`vm/reserved-name?`) | `:reserved-name` |\n   401\t| E2 | **free part agrees with the task**: with `C = (set (mapcat params (chain (body pc))))` the lexically bound names at that pc, `(apply dissoc bindings C) = (apply dissoc (:free-env task) C)` as maps of `V`; the chain of a return frame is that of its own `pc`. A key of `bindings` outside `C` that the free environment lacks, or a differing value, is a defect | `:free-env-mismatch` |\n   402\t\n   403\t**Pending and contexts.**\n   404\t\n   405\t| # | Rule | Kind |\n   406\t|---|---|---|\n   407\t| P1 | `context :wait` requires `:yin.k/pending` present; `:captured` and `:parked` require it absent | `:pending-presence` |\n   408\t| P2 | (`:wait`) the pending's reason is admitted by `inst(pc−1)` (act) or `inst(site)` (tail): `:stream-next → :next`; `:stream-put → :put`; `:ffi-call → :ffi, :ffi-request`; `:call → :next :put :ffi :ffi-request :link-request :link-response :install`; `:park` and `:current-continuation` admit none (frozen §4.1; `wire-of-kind`, `handoff.cljc:491-504`; ucf-revisions §8) | `:reason-mismatch` |\n   409\t| P3 | (`:captured`) the frame is an `act` and `inst(pc−1)` is `:current-continuation` | `:captured-site` |\n   410\t| P4 | (`:parked`) either `inst(pc−1)` is `:park` (an `act`), or `(:parked-key task) ∈ (:ffi-call-ids task)` and the frame is an `act` with `inst(pc−1) = :ffi-call` or a `tail` whose `inst(site)` is a tail `:call` (bookkeeping, evaluator §1.6) | `:parked-site` |\n   411\t\n   412\tRule E2 is the correction the review required (§4.4): a merged `E`\n   413\tcannot be split into free and lexical parts without the task's free\n   414\tenvironment, so the carrier carries it and the validator checks that\n   415\tevery `E` agrees with it off the lexical names. Nothing here reads a\n   416\tstack depth, a stack base or a `live` vector.\n   417\t\n   418\t### 3.3 Where and when the validator runs\n   419\t\n   420\t**DECIDED** (carrier order kept: draft §8, step 7 after step 6; the\n   421\treview's ruling). On **lower**: gate (1), structure (2), graph (3),\n   500\t4. `W = {virt(pc−1, s) ↦ V : [s V] ∈ regs}`; the kernel's `live` is the\n   501\t   physical image of `live-out*(pc−1) − {phys(rd)}`, so `(keys W) =\n   502\t   saved(pc, rd)`, which rule A5/A6 then checks.\n   503\t5. `E` = §4.4 from the entry's `frames` and `store-of`, at `body(pc)`.\n   504\t6. `K`: for each continuation frame `f`, **independently**: its\n   505\t   `return-pc` is absolute in the kernel's concatenated code space, so\n   506\t   first its image row `rowₖ = (image-row images return-pc)` and relative\n   507\t   `pcₖ = return-pc − offsetₖ`, then `Aₖ` of that row (frames may cross\n   508\t   images: a module closure called from another image returns into its\n   509\t   caller's image), `rdₖ = (code/rd (nth vₖ (dec pcₖ)))` from `Aₖ`, never\n   510\t   `f.dest`; `Wₖ = {virt_{Aₖ}(pcₖ−1, s) ↦ V : [s V] ∈ f.regs}`; `Eₖ` = §4.4\n   511\t   from `f.frames` and `f.store-of` at `body(pcₖ)` in `Aₖ`.\n   512\t7. pending: the engine fields of the entry, as `lift-pending!` maps them\n   752\treference run's normalised result; where a row says \"executable\" it runs\n   753\ton all three lanes; \"synthetic\" means the frame is built by hand and\n   754\tjudged by `frame/defect` only, because no program reaches it on the\n   755\tlanded or stage-2 evaluator.\n   756\t\n   757\t| # | Row | Program (inside each segment) | How parked / satisfied | State, pending | Expected after satisfy | Executable? |\n   758\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   759\t| 1 | blocked read | `(let1 s (stream/make 4) (let1 c (cursor-of s) (let1 a (next-of c) (cat (cat [] a) (next-of c)))))`, `\"A\"` appended before the run | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next` | `[\"A\" \"B\"]` | yes |\n   760\t| 2 | blocked write | `(stream-put w \"v\")` on a one-slot stream warmed with `:warmed` | take one | act, `:put` with retained `\"v\"` | `\"v\"` landed | yes |\n   761\t| 3 | FFI sent | `(dao.stream.apply/call :op/echo \"hello\")` | append the success response | act, `:ffi` | `\"echo!\"` | 4b stage 2 |\n   762\t| 4 | FFI retained | as 3 with a one-slot, warmed call-in | free the slot, then answer | act, `:ffi-request` | `\"echo!\"` | 4b stage 2 |\n   763\t| 5 | effectful call, non-tail, stream | `(cat [:ordinary] (stream/next! c))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next` | `[:ordinary \"B\"]` | yes (stage 1 has streams; `stream/next!` is the stream module's) |\n   764\t| 6 | **effectful call, tail, stream** | `((fn [u] (stream/next! c)) 0)` with the inner call `:tail? true` | append `\"B\"` | **tail**, `:next` | `\"B\"` delivered through `K` | yes |\n   765\t| 7 | link request phase | `(require 'host.mod)` parked **before** the request append succeeds (one-slot, warmed request stream) | free the slot, then answer `:ok` | act, `:link-request` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n   766\t| 8 | link response phase | `(require 'host.mod)` polling (request appended) | append the `:ok` response | act, `:link-response` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n   767\t| 9 | **link, tail** | `((fn [u] (require 'host.mod)) 0)` tail | as 8 | **tail**, `:link-response` | `'host.mod` through `K` | 4b stage 2 |\n   768\t| 10 | install, child running | `(require 'host.mod)` where `host.mod`'s body reads a stream the test has not fed, so the child is `:blocked` and the parent's wait is `:install` | feed the child's stream | act, `:install` + install entry, child kind `:blocked`, phase `:running` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n   769\t| 11 | install, child parked | as 10 with the child body executing `:park` | resume the child by id | act, `:install`, child kind `:parked`, phase `:parked` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n   770\t| 12 | install, tail | `((fn [u] (require 'host.mod)) 0)` tail with 10's child | as 10 | **tail**, `:install` | `'host.mod` through `K` | 4b stage 2 |\n   771\t| 13 | explicit park | `(vm/park)` | `(vm/resume pid \"back\")` beside | parked record, root `:parked` | `\"back\"` | yes |\n   772\t| 14 | reified capture live in a window | `(let1 k (vm/current-continuation) (cat (cat [] k) (next-of c)))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `k` is a `:reified` value in `W` | `[:continuation \"B\"]` normalised | yes |\n   773\t| 15 | capture invoked after lower | `(let1 k (vm/current-continuation) (if (= :first (next-of c)) (k :second) :done))`; parked at the read; after lower append `:first` | the invocation delivers `:second` into `k`'s `rd`, so the `if` re-tests | act, `:next` | `:done` (the second test sees `:second`) | yes |\n   774\t| 16 | nested capture | `(let1 k1 (vm/current-continuation) (let1 k2 (vm/current-continuation) (cat (cat (cat [] k1) k2) (next-of c))))` | append `\"B\"` | act; `k2`'s act window holds `k1` (a `:reified` inside a `:reified`'s window) | `[:continuation :continuation \"B\"]` | yes |\n   775\t| 17 | module context, blocked inside a module closure | `host.mod` exports `f = (fn [c] (stream/next! c))`; root: `(f c)` after `(require 'host.mod)` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`, `E` carries `store-of host.mod` | `\"B\"` | 4b stage 2 (link) |\n   776\t| 18 | module-store snapshot | `parked-module-store-cursors` (`lift_support.cljc:310-333`): an explicit park whose module store holds two cursors named by a module closure | resume | parked record; `:module-store` row | the cursors' cells | yes |\n   777\t| 19 | halt | `(lit 42)` | — | result | `42` | yes |\n   778\t| 20 | **tail-effect halt** | `((fn [c] (stream/next! c)) cursor)` in tail position at the root (empty `K`) | append `\"B\"` | tail, `:next` | halts with `\"B\"`, env free of `store-of` | yes |\n   779\t| 21 | **free-env shadowing** (the review's row) | initial free env `{x 99}`; `(let1 f (fn [] x) ((fn [x] (f (next-of c))) 1))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `E` at the read binds `x` to 1; root `free-env` carries `x 99` | the lowered `f` returns `99` (not nil, not 1) on every lane; **the one row the earlier design would have failed** | yes |\n   780\t| 22 | nil-valued live register | `(f nil (next-of c))` with `f = cat`: the `nil` operand is evaluated **before** the read and is live across it | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `W` has a present key with `[:lit nil]` | `[nil \"B\"]` | yes |\n   781\t| 23 | tail FFI bookkeeping | a `tail` parked record under a call id | — | parked, context `:parked`, bookkeeping clause of P4 | validator accepts; tampering `site` to a non-tail call is `:parked-site` | **synthetic**: no primitive returns an FFI effect through a tail `:call` today (evaluator §1.6) |\n   782\t| 24 | `act` FFI bookkeeping | 3's parked bookkeeping record under its call id | — | parked, P4 bookkeeping | validator accepts | 4b stage 2 |\n   842\tinput, cells as identities); replace every stream marker's identity and\n   843\tdescriptor by a placeholder determined by the marker's first occurrence\n   844\tin a fixed traversal of the abstract task (root slots in table order,\n   845\twaits in order, cells by body); run the canonical numbering (draft §6);\n   846\t**re-emit every row** and recompute every id; compare root ids. The\n   847\tprocedure is deterministic and renaming-invariant like the numbering it\n   848\treuses, and it is never used outside the harness.\n   849\t\n   850\t### 5.6 Static checks the harness runs once per corpus segment\n   851\t\n   852\t1. `frame/defect` on every frame the reference lane mints: nil.\n   853\t2. For every **reachable** parking pc `p` of `v`: `(analysis/saved a\n   854\t   (inc p) rd)` has no member `≥ k(body(p))` and does not contain `rd`.\n   855\t3. Register layout: at every reachable boundary pc `p`, `virt(p, s)` is\n   856\t   single-valued on the physical image of `live-out*(p)`; the `live`\n   857\t   operand of `R[p]` equals the sorted physical image of `live-out*(p) −\n   858\t   {phys(rd)}`, which is `[]` for a tail call (phase-5 §2.5).\n   859\t4. Stack layout: the k-th non-push instruction of `H` has the mnemonic\n   860\t   family of `v[k]` for every `k`; counts agree.\n   861\t5. Stack layout: `(set (stack-layout p)) = (analysis/saved a (inc p)\n   862\t   rd)` for every reachable **non-tail** parking pc `p`.\n   863\t6. `E` reconstruction: at every safepoint reached, the layout's `E`\n   864\t   equals the reference lane's `E` (values normalised), including rows\n   865\t   21 and 22 and the `:duplicate-param`, `:nested-closure`,\n   866\t   `:nested-lambdas` programs.\n   867\t7. Closure reconstruction: canonical ↔ positional closures round-trip on\n   868\t   the `\"closure value\"` and `\"higher order\"` B0 rows and\n   310\t(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n   311\t  \"A real machine parked at an explicit park whose module store for\n   312\t   'host.mod holds two cursor references nothing else reaches, named by\n   313\t   a module closure in the task store -- the shape a lowered module\n   314\t   closure has, its environment naming the module whose store it runs\n   315\t   against -- so the module-store snapshot's walk is the first place\n   316\t   either cell is minted.\"\n   317\t  []\n   318\t  (let [m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n   319\t                            (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n   320\t                                  (then (def! 'mod (lit 1))\n   321\t                                        (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park})\n   322\t                                             (v 'mod))))))\n   323\t        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n   324\t        seg (:segment (first (vals (:parked machine))))\n   325\t        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n   326\t                            {:type :closure, :params [], :entry 0,\n   327\t                             :segment seg,\n   328\t                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n   329\t    (assoc machine\n   330\t           :store (assoc (:store machine) 'mod clo)\n   331\t           :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1, 'd c2}})))\n   332\t\n   333\t\n   334\t(defn halted-with-cursors\n   335\t  \"A halted machine whose result is `(f c1 c2)` for the two fresh cursor\n   336\t   references nothing else reaches: the result walk is the first place\n   337\t   either cell is minted.\"\n   338\t  [f]\n   339\t  (let [{:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors (halted-machine))]\n   340\t    (assoc machine :value (f c1 c2))))\n   341\t\n   342\t\n   343\t(defn halted-result-closure\n   344\t  \"A halted machine whose result is a module closure -- its environment\n   345\t   naming 'host.mod -- and whose 'host.mod module store holds two cursor\n314:;;   so that conj appends rather than prepends.\n399:           (pure 'conj conj [1 2 :variadic])\n790:         emit! (fn [e attr val] (swap! datoms conj [e attr val t m]))\n808:                (when pre-eid (swap! seen-eids conj pre-eid))\n1290:                  (swap! positions conj\n1298:                  (swap! metadata conj [origin root path k v]))\n1303:                    :node (visit value (conj path pos))\n1305:                             (visit child (conj path [pos i])))\n1509:                                       (let [on-path' (conj on-path id)]\n1669:                                 (map (fn [[step cid]] [(conj path step) cid])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
